    "answer": {
      "short": "$1:3$",
      "worked": "Bottle A has $3+7=10$ parts.\n$$\\begin{align*}10\\text{ parts}&=1\\text{ L}\\\\1\\text{ part}&=1\\div10=0.1\\text{ L}\\\\\\text{Cordial in A}&=3\\times0.1=0.3\\text{ L}\\\\\\text{Water in A}&=7\\times0.1=0.7\\text{ L}\\end{align*}$$\nBottle B has $1+4=5$ parts.\n$$\\begin{align*}5\\text{ parts}&=1\\text{ L}\\\\1\\text{ part}&=1\\div5=0.2\\text{ L}\\\\\\text{Cordial in B}&=1\\times0.2=0.2\\text{ L}\\\\\\text{Water in B}&=4\\times0.2=0.8\\text{ L}\\end{align*}$$\nCombine the corresponding volumes.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Total cordial}&=0.3+0.2=0.5\\text{ L}\\\\\\text{Total water}&=0.7+0.8=1.5\\text{ L}\\\\\\text{Cordial : water}&=0.5:1.5\\\\\\text{Cordial : water}&=1:3\\end{align*}$$",
